Step 0 supports a build, but only on Track B. I’m using Section 4’s native probe-split construction (Theorem 4.3): any connected bipartite graph becomes a partitioned probe split graph by taking one bipartition class as non-probes and completing it to a clique. The paper’s general problem remains NP-complete there, but the generated subclass deliberately has a polynomial reference route—an \(s\)-\(t\) min-cut followed by exact \(GF(2)\) fitting—so I will report that route and its measured cost rather than make a false distributional Track A claim. The compact witness route is a parity-kernel invariant encoded in the vertex labels.
