A broader 1,000-seed construction audit found every planted and compact certificate valid and every canonical key distinct. It also exposed a useful caveat: the basic spectral bisection recovered 90/100, not 100/100, because the original circulant pieces have weak internal spectral gaps. I’m tightening the construction to a union of edge-disjoint Hamiltonian cycles. This preserves inverse generation and regularity, gives a direct internal-cut lower bound, and makes the mandated spectral reference audit representative rather than accidentally seed-dependent.
