codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track B affine matching-cut generator based on the paper’s probe-split construction in Theorem 14. The paper confirms that \(d\)-Cut remains NP-complete on probe split graphs, while this generated subclass has an explicitly disclosed polynomial reference algorithm. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.22351)

Key results:

- All local gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four adversarial heuristics: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, median 23,275 operations.
- Compact invariant route: 228 operations.
- Answer size: 51 characters, 25 elements.
- Canonicalization now covers arbitrary invertible \(\mathrm{GF}(2)\) basis changes.
- Additional 200-instance determinism and structural audit passed.

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/gen_2505_22351.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

One external blocker remains: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every fresh oracle call. Consequently, all three oracle arms have zero scored attempts, and the family cannot honestly be declared hardened or submitted until the quota is restored and `harden.py` is rerun.
