codex
Implemented and locally verified the Track B generator.

Key results:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/gen_2505_22351.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/selftest_report.json): all G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/README.md), including corrected paper references to Observation 2.1 and Theorems 1.4, 3.1, 3.2, and 4.3.
- G4: 0 valid guesses in 200,000 structured samples.
- Independent 200-seed audit: planted, compact, min-cut, and spectral routes succeeded 200/200; all four adversarial heuristics succeeded 0/200.
- Track B mechanical route: median 23,275 operations; compact parity route: 228 operations.
- Answer: 51 serialized characters and 25 atoms.

The construction uses the paper’s native probe-split matching-cut objects under Theorem 4.3, with affine labels serving only as compressed certificate encoding. See the [paper’s full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2505.22351v1).

One external blocker remains: every official bare, hinted, and placebo hardening request returned OpenRouter HTTP 403, “Key limit exceeded,” before a model answered. The script-owned error evidence is preserved in:

- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2505.22351/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Consequently, the generator is locally complete but must not be claimed or submitted as oracle-hardened until those three harness runs are repeated with restored OpenRouter quota. No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure blocker, not a G/H/V failure.
