371:\section{Polynomial-Time Results}\label{s-poly}
375:Our proofs are based on combining colour-processing with the observation that we can guess the closed neighbourhood of any set of size at most some constant~$c$: this will lead to only $\mathcal{O}(2^cn^{cd})$ branches, due to the fact that any vertex can have at most $d$ neighbours of the opposite colour. In our algorithms we choose a constant number of constant-sized sets in such a way that afterwards the whole input graph is coloured.
